      "body": "The checkpoint converter crashes with `--debug` on ZeRO-3 checkpoints.\n\n`_zero3_merge_trainable_params` receives each rank's optimizer groups as a list and the debug block treats it as a tensor, reading `.shape` and `.numel()` off the list. Print the per-group shapes instead, the way the ZeRO-2 debug block above it already does, and drop the `avail_numel` reassignment: it recomputed, wrongly, a value the top of the function already has.\n\nTests: `DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu python -m pytest tests/unit/checkpoint/test_convert_checkpoint.py -k 'not TestCheckpointConvert' -q`. Debug export fails before. Five converter tests pass after. A separate real ZeRO-3 Adam step with two parameter groups, checkpoint save and debug export produces matching weights. Changed-file pre-commit passes. Apple M2 Pro CPU, PyTorch 2.10, one-rank Gloo; no GPU run.",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vineethsaivs"
            },
            "body": "Could a maintainer approve CI for this PR? The focused regression tests and repository lint checks pass locally.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-15T23:01:02Z",
            "databaseId": 5689244693,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-15T23:01:02Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8530#issuecomment-5689244693"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vineethsaivs"
            },
            "body": "Good catch, added to the description: the shadowed `avail_numel` also fed the `offset != avail_numel` sanity check at the end, so under `--debug` that check was comparing against the wrong number. Thanks for running it.",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-21T06:50:28Z",
            "databaseId": 5756523298,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-21T06:50:28Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8530#issuecomment-5756523298"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vineethsaivs"
            },
            "body": "Correcting myself: that reassignment never actually ran. The `.shape` print above it is the first statement in the `debug` block and raises the same AttributeError, so the final `offset != avail_numel` check always used the correct sum from the top of the function. It was a stale line, not a wrong comparison. I have taken that claim back out of the description.",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-21T06:51:37Z",
            "databaseId": 5756534417,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-21T06:51:37Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8530#issuecomment-5756534417"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "alanhuangyoo"
            },
            "body": "You're right, the print dies first so that line never ran. My mistake, thanks for checking.",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-21T09:02:27Z",
            "databaseId": 5757968542,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-21T09:02:27Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8530#issuecomment-5757968542"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "alanhuangyoo"
            },
            "body": "This looks right to me. avail_numel is already defined at the top of the function and the check at the end uses it, so dropping the reassignment is safe.",
