            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "alanhuangyoo"
            },
            "body": "Ran your test on CPU both ways: master dies at the same `AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'shape'`, passes on this branch.\n\nOne thing worth adding to the description: the `avail_numel` line you removed wasn't only crashing. It replaced the correct group sum from the top of the function with `fp32_flat_groups[0].numel()`, and `avail_numel` is what the `offset != avail_numel` check at the end compares against, so with `--debug` that check was looking at the wrong number too.\n\nThe zero-2 debug block at :317 already prints shapes per group, so this just brings stage 3 in line.\n",
